.th CLRM VIII 5/31/77
.sh NAME
clrm \*- clear mode of i-node
.sh SYNOPSIS
.bd /etc/clrm
filesystem i-number ...
.sh DESCRIPTION
.it Clrm
writes a zero in the two byte mode of the associated
i-node numbered
.it i-number.
The
.it filesystem
argument must be a special file name referring
to a device containing a file system.
More than one
.it i-number
may be given.
After
.it clrm,
any blocks in the affected file will show up as
``missing'' in a
.it check
of the
.it filesystem.
.s3
The primary purpose of this routine is to remove
a file which does not appear in a directory.
Internal checks are performed on each
.it i-number
to protect the
.it filesystem
against clearing either a directory or a special file.
.s3
Since
.it clrm
does not destroy the i-node's original disk block address when
invoked, the i-node, if cleared by mistake, may then be
salvaged more efficiently.
.sh "SEE ALSO"
check(VIII), clri(VIII)
